o move their annual fiesta from January 21 to March 14 after voting 6 to 1. They also asked the treasurer to release 45,000 pesos for repairs before the new date.\n\nThe question is asking for the date when the fiesta will be held. The key information here is that the vote was to move the fiesta from January 21 to March 14. So even though they had a previous date of January 21, the decision was made to change it to March 14. \n\nI need to make sure there's no trick in the question. Sometimes problems might mention dates but have some other condition that affects the final answer. For example, maybe the repairs needed before the new date would affect when they can actually hold the fiesta. But the problem states that the members voted to move it to March 14 and asked for the release of funds \"before\" the new date. However, the question is just asking on what date the fiesta will be held, not considering any delays or additional requirements beyond the vote itself.\n\nSo based solely on the information given, the answer should be March 14. The fact that they had to release money before that date doesn't change the official date of the event once it's been decided by the council. Therefore, the fiesta will be held on March 14.\n<\/think>\n\nThe fiesta will be held on **March 14**.","reasoning_chars":0,"raw":"<think>\nOkay, let's see. The problem is about the Barangay San Isidro council meeting on Tuesday where they decided to move their annual fiesta from January 21 to March 14 after voting 6 to 1. They also asked the tre
